  "term": "effortless attention",
  "definition": "In James’s account, effortless attention is the usual, smooth form of attending in which thought follows its natural course without strain or a sense of willful reinforcement. It contrasts with effortful attention, which is felt when competing interests interrupt this easy flow and attention must be held against distraction.",
